    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63822&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "FSUS ESE Paraprofessional – Secondary (Full-time, OPS)",
      "description": "FSUS ESE Paraprofessional – Secondary (Full-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63822 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities The paraprofessional will work under the direction of certified staff to support academic and behavioral needs of students in the classroom and other school settings. This role involves assisting with instructional activities, supervising students, and providing one-on-one or small group support to help students achieve academic success and positive social outcomes. Assist the classroom teacher in implementing lesson plans and instructional activities. Work with individual students or small groups to reinforce learning concepts introduced by the teacher. Support students with special needs by implementing IEP accommodations and modifications as directed. Assist with classroom management by monitoring student behavior and promoting a safe and respectful environment. Help with the preparation of instructional materials and classroom organization. Supervise students in various settings, including classrooms, hallways, cafeterias, playgrounds, and school events. Provide clerical support such as photocopying, filing, and data entry as needed. Maintain confidentiality and demonstrate professionalism at all times. Participate in training and professional development activities as required. Qualifications High school diploma. Experience working with children or in an educational setting is a plus. Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Ability to follow directions, take initiative, and respond flexibly to changing needs. Patience, compassion, and a commitment to supporting student learning and well-being. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree, two years of college (60 credit hours), or successful completion of a state-approved paraprofessional assessment. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. Contact Info Jaye Corbett University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=59627&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried – Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL)",
      "description": "Family Physician/Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried – Multiple Positions (Family Medicine & Rural Health - Medicine - Tallahassee, FL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 59627 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Family Medicine & Rural Health Responsibilities The Department of Family Medicine and Rural Health is seeking academic family medicine physicians to fill full-time 12-month open rank faculty positions at a minimum rank of either Assistant or Associate Professor, dependent upon qualifications and experience. This is a clinical position and is not tenure-earning eligible. The positions will involve substantial teaching and supervision of health professional students as well as assisting in the delivery of an innovative, integrated curriculum and practice in a clinical facility. The positions will include around 40% direct patient care at an affiliated primary care practice (credentialing required). The Department has research interests in the areas of health equity, community health, rural health, and innovative health care. Qualifications Applicants must have a doctoral degree (MD or DO) in an appropriate field from an accredited institution and personal and professional goals which are consistent with the mission of the FSU College of Medicine. Applicants must have completed an approved U.S. Residency Program. Applicants must have Board Certification in Family Medicine or other acceptable discipline and participate in maintenance of certification. Applicants should have relevant academic, clinical, and professional experience, excellent skills in communication and collaboration, and be passionate about the field of family medicine and rural health. Additional specific requirements and qualifications include: Must possess, or obtain within 90 days of hire, a valid Florida license to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) Healthcare Provider Certification by a certifying agency, or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to foster an educational environment conducive to patient-centered medical student and physician assistant education. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Post-job offer, but prior to hire, the following will be required: Documentation of current PPD (Purified Protein Derivative) test as performed by a qualified physician reporting negative results within the past six months. Documentation of physical examination completed by a qualified healthcare provider/physician within the past six months. Within 30 days of hire, must provide: Documentation of vaccination for Tetanus within the last 10 years. Proof of immunization OR positive titers for Hepatitis B. Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching medical students and primary care research is highly desired. Clinical experience post-residency/fellowship is desired. Scholarly interest, knowledge and experience with health equity or community-based health outcomes or clinical research is desired. Knowledge and experience with medical informatics is desired. Other Information The Florida State University College of Medicine (FSU COM) has a focused mission of training patient-centered physicians devoted to the needs of rural, underserved, minority, and elderly populations. FSU COM is very “Family Medicine friendly” with family physicians holding several key administrative positions including Dean of the College. As a community-based medical school, FSU COM is particularly well-suited for conducting research in primary care and community settings. Contact Info Ms. Ute Sartin, Assistant Director, Email: ute.sartin@med.fsu.edu Ms. Danyel White, Sr. Administrative Specialist, Email: danyel.white@med.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applications should include the following: Cover letter of interest Curriculum vitae Letters of Reference (refer to steps below) 2 - 3 page teaching, mentoring, and service statement that describes prior experiences and future plans 2 - 3 page research statement that briefly summarizes your significant research accomplishments and describes your future research plans Request Letters of Reference This position requires that you have 3 - 4 confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Applications will be reviewed as received. This job opening serves to recruit for two positions. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63834&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Office Assistant - College of Fine Arts (Full-time, OPS)",
      "description": "Office Assistant - College of Fine Arts (Full-time, OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63834 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Dean's Office - College of Fine Arts Responsibilities Responsible for greeting and assisting customers (visitors, students, special guests, faculty, and staff) of the office of the Dean via personal, telephone, and email interactions. Serves as the first point of contact to accurately direct inquiries throughout the Dean's Office and the College. Supports general office workflow. Performs a variety of standard clerical tasks such as filing (physical and electronic), record retention, mail distribution, phone support, data entry, basic report preparation, data reconciliation, document creation, and editing. Orders and receives office supplies and performs inventory functions. Assist with booking and processing travel for Dean’s Office staff . Assist with events coordination including set up and tear down of events. Works with Communications team to assist with social media and content writing and editing. Maintains the appearance of Dean's Office and shared spaces within the Facility for Art Research building by organizing supplies and paperwork. Delivers and retrieves materials to and from the College and University offices both on and off campus. Provides limited direct support to the Dean under the supervision of the Dean’s Assistant. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Basic knowledge of computer applications (ex. Microsoft Outlook, Work, Excel, PowerPoint, or equivalents on other platforms). Ability to perform routine errands both on and off campus to the College of Fine Arts buildings. Ability to function independently with minimal to moderate supervision. Preferred Qualifications Experience in an office setting requiring advanced customer service skills. Experience with writing and editing in relation to public facing communications. Knowledge of office practices, procedures, and etiquette. Experience proactively addressing situations independently. Experience with events management. Experience with social media platforms. Excellent organizational skills. Multitasking and time-management skills. Hands-on experience with office equipment including fax machines, copiers and printers. Other Information The Florida State University College of Fine Arts is a place where learning and creativity are nurtured through instruction, research, and practice. The College includes faculty, students, and professionals that function as an arts conservatory within a major university. The College offers degree programs in Art, Art Education, Art History, Dance, Interior Architecture and Design, and Theatre. The College also houses several non-academic units including the Museum of Fine Arts, the Facility for Arts Research, and the Maggie Allesee National Center for Choreography (MANCC). University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $17 - $19 per hour, commensurate with education and experience. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . If not otherwise specified, the schedule is Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. This position is located on site at the Facility for Art Research - FAR (3216 Sessions Rd, Tallahassee, FL 32303). Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
