    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63564&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "IT Support Specialist",
      "description": "IT Support Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63564 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of I nformation Technology Services (ITS) Responsibilities Responsible as end user technical support for the Athletics Department. Responsible for supporting desktop systems, software, and hardware for the Athletics department. Configuration of systems of varying complexity and troubleshooting of advanced technical issues. Provides support for all desktops, laptops, mobile devices, printers, and software systems used in Athletics. Main point of contact for technical support within the department to initiate and resolve issues that arise at multiple sites. Provides on-site support as well as support via phone and email. Capable of working in an environment containing potentially confidential information and ensuring user data is provided resiliency and protected from malicious software. Responsible for managing Athletics inventory for technology including adding new assets and managing old or non-functional equipment. Administrator of Mobile Device Management solution which tracks all Athletics mobile devices. Administrator of Athletics deployment solution for imaging of Windows Workstations. Provides on-site support for essential services provided by Information Technology Services such as network connectivity, email, and Active Directory Services. Supplements University provided anti-virus software by updating and patching Athletics systems to prevent exploitation. Serves as principle point of contact to answer inquiries and serves as liaison between users and Information Technology Services and other departments providing services to Athletics. Identifies department needs and correctly and accurately logging support cases or support request to the appropriate service provider. Serves as on-site support for hardware or software provided by a third party vendors. Must be able to work with outside groups to achieve resolution of technical issues to meet department deadlines. Responsible for technology support for events as determined by the Director of Information Technology Services. This will require on-site or on-call support for home Athletics events. Will coordinate with visiting media and production staff for connectivity with Athletics network resources, support for Athletics game day technology, and support for Athletics staff during home events. Will work to improve game day operations and the efficiency of technology at Athletics venues. Responsible for special projects as assigned by the Director of Technology Support Services. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to four years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. Other Information This position provides IT Support to the Athletics Department, Seminole Boosters, and Seminole Productions. It also supports third party companies, like Legends, and Aramark. The staff is heavily involved with Athletics events and special events (as of recently). We are on-site during most athletics events. If it has data or electricity, we are involved. This includes OPS Students, OPS engineers, and normal full-time employees. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? The ideal candidate is someone with IT support experience and enjoys sports. What is a typical day in this position? Receive and resolve support requests. In some cases you will also work athletic events. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63817&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar (FSU Humanities Center) - Multiple Positions",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar (FSU Humanities Center) - Multiple Positions Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63817 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Humanities Center | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Humanities Center at Florida State University (FSU) invites applications for the position of Postdoctoral Scholar. We anticipate making four appointments for 2027. These are full-time, non-tenure-track positions with an anticipated start date in August 2027. The initial appointment is for 12 months, with the possibility of renewal (for up to 2 years total in the position). The teaching load is one course per semester. Specialization areas include Classics, Philosophy, Religion, History, Modern Languages & Linguistics, and English. Successful applicants will be located in the department matching their specialty. Scholars are expected to be in residence for the duration of their fellowship, attend the lectures, conferences, workshops, and other events held at the Center, and deliver by the end of their appointment a scholarly article, exhibit, or book relevant to the Center’s theme. The Humanities Center theme for 2027-2029 is “Authenticity.” The Center invites projects that examine how the genuine, the original, and the true have been defined, contested, and performed across periods. Possible areas include forgery and provenance, sincerity and the self, translation and adaptation, historical reconstruction and performance practice, the authority of sacred and canonical texts, mimesis and expropriation, and the challenges posed to authenticity by reproduction and artificial intelligence. Project fit with the theme is a selection criterion. For more information about the FSU Humanities Center, please visit our website . Qualifications A Ph.D. (or highest degree appropriate) in any field of the humanities from an accredited institution other than FSU is required, as well as demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in specialty area and promise of contributing to exploration of the Center’s topic. Applicants must have received the Ph.D. no earlier than August 2022, and it must be conferred before August 2027. Contact Info Inquiries about this search should be directed to the Humanities Center . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Applications should include a cover letter that addressing the applicant’s interest in investigating the Center’s topic, CV, writing sample (max of 35 pages), and statements of teaching and research. Applicants should discuss how they would fit into one of the departments listed above, including by outlining their teaching capabilities. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The deadline to apply is January 4, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63810&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Director, Administrative Services (Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Program Director, Administrative Services (Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63810 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine - College of Medicine Responsibilities Program Director, Administrative & Financial Operations: Join the leadership team of the Department of Behavioral Sciences and Social Medicine (BSSM) as a strategic partner to the Department Chair. In this impactful role, you'll help lead departmental operations, financial planning, staffing strategy, and administrative services that support teaching, research, and service initiatives. What you'll do: Partner with the Chair on departmental strategy, operations, and organizational effectiveness. Lead budget planning, financial analysis, forecasting, and resource management across multiple funding sources. Provide operational leadership for HR, procurement, travel, and administrative functions serving approximately 140 faculty and staff across a growing department and its affiliated programs and centers. Supervise and develop administrative team members while driving service excellence. Interpret university policies and implement process improvements that enhance efficiency and compliance. Deliver data-driven reports and recommendations to support informed decision-making. Why you'll love this role: This is an opportunity to make a meaningful impact in a dynamic academic environment where your leadership will directly support faculty success, research growth, operational excellence, and the department's long-term strategic goals. We're looking for a collaborative, solutions-oriented leader who thrives in a fast-paced environment and enjoys translating strategy into action. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to administrative services; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to ten years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Georgia Arnold Program Director University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63821&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - (NHMFL)",
      "description": "Research Faculty I, 12 Month Salaried - (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63821 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Responsibilities The Magnet Science and Technology Division of the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) is seeking an exceptional individual for a Research Faculty position for magnet design and system analysis. A primary responsibility will be development of systems (including both hardware and software, LabVIEW) to detect quench of superconducting magnets and discharge the stored energy of those magnets (up to 50 MJ) quickly, safely, and in a reliable and cost-effective manner. Another key responsibility includes electromagnetic, structural, and thermal analysis and design of new and existing high magnetic field systems employing resistive conductors and/ or low and high temperature superconductors. Specific targets as outlined in our strategic plan are a 40 Tall-superconducting magnet system and high-field HTS inserts up to 60 T. The incumbent will be organizing and carrying out work that includes numerical simulation (COMSOL, ANSYS, Vector Fields, Fortran, Matlab, C++, etc.), system and component testing, data analysis, among other tasks like providing studies and reports, which enables the department to develop a deep understanding of advanced high-field magnet systems and successfully design and construct such magnets. The position will play a leading role in the development of next-generation high-field magnet systems. Presenting results in international conferences and publishing in peer-reviewed journals is expected. Preparation of reports and technical papers is required. This position is flexible in the emphasis on either numerical analysis or instrumentation. Qualifications Requirements include a minimum of a Ph.D in engineering, physics, or a related field, or equivalent qualification based on professional experience and demonstrated record of achievement in research. Preferred Qualifications We are seeking a candidate who is highly motivated and eager to work flexibly and creatively in a multi-disciplinary team environment developing a deep understanding of new technologies and specific magnets. Experience with Electronics is a plus. Good communication skills and the ability to interact constructively with physicists, engineers, designers, technicians, and procurement personnel are required. It is preferred, but not required, that candidate should have at least two years of previous experience in instrumentation electronics. A strong background in the fields of cryogenics, superconducting materials, magnets and their design, especially HTS magnets is preferred. Contact Info Tom Painter , 850-567-7320 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Careers link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63678&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist - UBA/College of Music",
      "description": "Accounting Specialist - UBA/College of Music Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63678 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department University Business Administrators - College of Music Responsibilities Responsible for performing professional fiscal activities at the College of Music (CoM), including travel, purchasing, and deposit accounting, with an emphasis on student-facing financial functions, including student group travel and tours, student travel grants, scholarships, course-enhancement initiatives, tuition waivers, and student finance communications. Responsible for day-to-day origination of travel authorizations, cash advances, and expense reports for student travel, including individual, small group, and large group trips/tours. Provides recommendations to support the travel initiatives developed to enhance and enrich the CoM student experience. Creates and maintains CoM-specific travel training guides, travel resources, and post-travel forms. Proactively communicates with International Travel, Safety, and Risk, and the University Clery Compliance Officer prior to CoM group travel. Routes student travel waivers prior to departure for all college-sanctioned student group travel. Reviews travel card transactions for accuracy and policy compliance. Maintains appropriate travel logs and regularly updates interested parties on the status of their upcoming travel and post-travel expense reports. Tracks and monitors purchasing activities at the CoM to ensure a sound environment of internal controls and compliance. Interprets and communicates policies to faculty, staff, and students. Makes recommendations regarding purchasing processes and advises on alternatives as needed, in particular to accommodate requests for purchase of course materials or in support of student entrepreneurial initiatives. Prepares and utilizes college-wide reports for tracking requisitions and purchase orders to ensure adherence to area budget allocations as well as timely transaction entry and payment processing. Communicates with internal stakeholders as necessary and ensures compliance with University policies and procedures. Serves as primary PCard holder for CoM Fiscal Office requests. Serves as backup to Sr. Accounting Specialist for faculty, staff, professional development, recruitment, and guest artist travel. Serves as backup PCard Proxy for the CoM, assisting with auditing and coding of departmental purchase card payments as needed. Serves as secondary liaison between College cardholders and FSU Procurement/PCard Admin. Enters and reconciles all foundation scholarship awards in FS4U. Collaborates with Sr. Accounting Specialist and Assistant Deans for Admissions & Recruitment and Finance & Administration, as well as the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Graduate Academic Program Specialist, and Assistant Dean for Undergraduate Programs to process and reconcile all academic year awards. Participates in unencumbered payment activities at the (CoM) to include origination of non-travel reimbursements in FSU Systems, payments to vendors via ePRF, and the PCard program. Identifies process enhancements in existing operations to improve efficiency and delegation throughout the the CoM Fiscal Office. Regularly reviews and takes necessary actions on PCard transactions, outstanding T-Card transactions, and aging travel requests, monitoring financial transactions and ensuring compliance with University policy and procedures. Serves as a key point of contact for College of Music (CoM) student inquiries pertaining to student financials, including account balances, award disbursements, tuition waivers, insurance subsidies, fee liability, scholarship status, tax liability, payment plans, and adjustments. Serves as a liaison among the CoM Fiscal Office, Office of Student Success, FSU Financial Aid, Student Finance, The Graduate School, and Payroll. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate should have the following skill and/or experience. Collaborative attitude and the ability to thrive working with faculty, students, guests, and staff. Excellent attention to detail, communication skills, and the ability to work independently. Ability to successfully prioritize, organize and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
