    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63805&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Digital Communications Specialist (Public Affairs & Communication - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Digital Communications Specialist (Public Affairs & Communication - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63805 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Public Affairs & Communication - College of Medicine Responsibilities Responsible for managing and enhancing the College's digital communications and web presence through content development, website administration, social media engagement, analytics, and compliance with university branding and accessibility standards to support goals and constituent engagement. Create and edit written, visual and multimedia content, including social media posts, blog content, graphics, short-form videos and animations. Monitor emerging trends and recommend innovative approaches to enhance audience engagement and brand visibility. Collaborate with college leadership, departments, programs and University Communications to support the development and implementation of digital communication strategies that enhance engagement with key constituent groups. Provide support for electronic communications, including email campaigns, electronic newsletters and other digital outreach efforts. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Content Creation & Social Media: Proficiency in developing, coordinating, and distributing multi-platform content (social media, blog posts, graphics, photography, short-form video, and animation) to promote college initiatives and strategic priorities. Web & Digital Administration: Experience managing website main pages, content management systems (CMS), and ensuring compliance with web standards, ADA/accessibility guidelines, SEO, and GEO. Analytics & Strategy: Ability to utilize analytics and reporting tools (such as Sprout Social) to evaluate communication effectiveness and guide continuous improvement. Software & Technical Proficiency: Advanced knowledge of computer applications and MS Office. Advanced knowledge of current media technology and trends, including documented proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Acrobat Professional, Dreamweaver). Soft Skills : Effective verbal and written communication, strong project management, ability to meet strict deadlines, and skill in establishing effective working relationships with leadership and external stakeholders. Contact Info Rita Am Office Administrator University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
