    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63788&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator - FSU Real Estate Center, Herbert Wertheim College of Business",
      "description": "Program Coordinator - FSU Real Estate Center, Herbert Wertheim College of Business Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63788 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Real Estate Center - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities Works in close coordination with the Real Estate Center's Executive Director to support the administrative needs and projects of the Center. Plans, coordinates, and executes Real Estate Center events including conferences, speaker series, student professional development events, symposia, advisory council meetings, partner visits, and receptions. Develops timelines, budgets, marketing materials, registration platforms, travel logistics, and vendor contracts. Oversees on-site execution and supervises student and volunteer staff. As needed, travels off campus to support Center events, both around the state and nationally. Serves as a primary contact for Real Estate students regarding Center programming, professional development, travel opportunities, and scholarship opportunities. Plans and manages logistics for student activities such as trainings, bootcamps, case competitions, corporate tours, conferences, and travel-based learning experiences. Handles financial processes for assigned activities, including budgeting, requisitions, purchase orders, contracts, invoicing, expense payments, and reconciliation in accordance with university and FSU Foundation procedures. Manages communication channels (Canvas, email campaigns, social media, newsletters) to increase student participation. Supervises graduate assistants and manages resume book/business card production for Real Estate students. Collaborates with Wertheim College of Business staff, faculty, and external partners to ensure compliance with university and Foundation policies related to budgeting, travel, contracts, and event execution. Executes the Real Estate Center’s industry outreach and marketing plan. Maintains communication with employers, executive board members, alumni, and corporate partners. Supports partner deliverables, sponsorship activities, and employer engagement initiatives in close coordination with the college’s Business Career Services office. Assists with alumni outreach and promotional projects. Organizes and maintains roster of current board members to include specific demographic information on each (sector, function, level, location, etc.), sends appropriate notices to members for service status along with invoice for payment of board commitments and follow up to ensure commitments are completed. Maintains accurate lists of nominated board members for future service, collects required references, etc. Works in accordance with established processes and procedures, and coordinates closely with the college’s UBA team, to ensure processing of invoices, expense payments, requisitions, and purchase orders. Monitors budgets and Foundation accounts in consultation with the Dean’s Office. Maintains Center records and calendars and liaises with college administrative units to support Center operations. Creates and maintains a robust tracking system of alumni and/or professionals interested in program and student engagement – data to include demographic details, industry related specifics, outreach and level of engagement preferred. Maintains accurate information regarding giving, sponsorships, engagement, etc. Serves as a primary contact for Real Estate Center visitors. Handles daily communication for the Center including managing email and phone inquiries and routing as appropriate. Handles mass correspondence on behalf of the Center. Manages the Center's mail, copying printing, and on campus errands. Performs other related duties as required and assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Amanda Chapman Assistant Director, Administrative Services FSU Real Estate Center University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . As needed travel required. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63800&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Service Desk Analyst I (Multiple Hires)",
      "description": "Service Desk Analyst I (Multiple Hires) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63800 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of Information Technology Services (ITS) Responsibilities This position is part of the ITS Campus Team. The College of Medicine’s Office of Information Technology, OIT or MED IT, serves to support the faculty, staff, and students in all areas requiring IT assistance, but specifically in these example areas: deployment of individual use computers, classroom technology, conference room technology, software support, administration of Audio Visual equipment and components, event support and live streaming, account support and maintenance, maintenance of departmental servers both on-premise and in the cloud, network support and troubleshooting, systems development and monitoring, development of specialized department software, database maintenance and support, IT purchasing and contract management, monitoring for cybersecurity threats, protection of privacy, and general IT consulting. Team members from MED IT have expertise in each of these areas and support the educational, research, clinical, and community outreach activities for the College of Medicine. Serves as a point of contact for the distribution and support of information technology resources owned and managed by the College of Medicine. Responsible for initial triage and troubleshooting of computer hardware and software issues. Uses automated help desk ticketing system and other record keeping procedures to properly document actions taken in a timely and efficient manner. Communicates solutions to end users by providing one-on-one resolution over the phone, electronic communication, and in-person. Collaborates with and escalates to other teams where necessary to resolve the end user's issue. Assists with administration and support of classrooms, computer labs, library and multi-media equipment. Assists with troubleshooting end-user issues relating to telephone system features and instruments, videoconferencing and remote connectivity of computers. Also assists with the administration of exams and ensuring computers are functioning properly for examinations. Images and deploys Windows and Mac devices in their appropriate management solutions. Educates end users on their proper use and documents their setups in our hardware inventory systems. Assists in the use and maintenance of printers. Works with end users to print posters and ships them out in a timely fashion where necessary. Assists in property inventory tracking. Monitors supplies and equipment inventories for help desk operations and communicates inventory needs with the Business Analyst. Properly processes equipment due for surplus, including erasing all data, and documenting in our inventory tracking system. Performs duties in compliance with ITS policies, guidelines, and processes pertaining to support requests, work orders, project management, change management, and incident management. Appropriately utilizes associated tools in accordance with ITS standards. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience or a post high school education and experience equal to two years. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in a fast-paced IT help desk environment Previous experience in IT-centric Customer Service Previous experience with ticketing systems such as Salesforce and TeamDynamix Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Ideally this candidate has previous IT experience and strong customer service skills. Enterprise experience is preferred but not required. If you are comfortable navigating and troubleshooting basic problems with a computer this will help you in this role. The candidate should be knowledgeable of applicable computer software, operating systems and hardware. The candidate should have familiarity with standard concepts, practices and procedures for computer support. The candidate should have the ability to prioritize and organize multiple work assignments in a high-speed work environment and apply fundamental problem-solving skills. What is a typical day in this position? We start each day going through our existing/new tickets. We assist walk ins and phone calls with various technical issues. We work in a fast-paced environment. In between tickets we work on upgrading older computers and various equipment. We also work on creating and updating new/existing knowledge base articles and training materials in our environment. What can I expect in the first 60-90 days? To be fully versed in our environment. This includes but is not limited to customer service skills in-person and over the phone, troubleshooting computers and other devices, managing our ticketing system, and imaging computers for new/existing faculty/staff/students. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61880&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Substitute Teacher (Part-time, OPS) (Panama City, FL) (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Substitute Teacher (Part-time, OPS) (Panama City, FL) (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61880 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Collegiate School at FSU Panama City is a developmental research laboratory charter school associated with the College of Education at Florida State University. In this capacity, The Collegiate School serves as a center for innovative instructional programming, research and program evaluation, and professional development solutions for the educational community. The mission of The Collegiate School at Florida State University Panama City is to provide rigorous academic studies and career development for students who aspire to meet the ever- changing and complex workplace demands of the 21st century. Resources and expertise available through Florida State University and the local community will prepare students to thrive in the competitive global market as they identify and pursue career goals through academic and career training. Responsibilities Substitutes for teachers grades 9-11. Works with teachers in the classroom to help students. Supervises the classroom in teacher’s absence. Completes paperwork under the teacher’s direction. May include other student supervisory duties as needed. Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. Contact Info Debbi Whitaker - d.whitaker@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63770&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate, and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate, and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63770 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate, and Legal Studies - Herbert Wertheim College of Business Responsibilities The Florida State University Herbert Wertheim College of Business invites applications for a full-time, specialized faculty position in the Department of Risk Management/Insurance, Real Estate, and Legal Studies, beginning Fall 2027. This is a non-tenure-track, non-tenure-earning position. The successful candidate will teach four courses per semester at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, primarily in the areas of business law and wealth management. Teaching assignments may include courses in business law, estate planning, wealth management, and other related areas. Specific course assignments will be determined based on the candidate's academic qualifications, professional expertise, teaching experience, and departmental needs. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, effectively engage students in the application of legal and business principles, and contribute to curriculum development and student learning. Service to the department, college, university, and profession is also expected. Qualifications Candidates must possess a terminal degree (Juris Doctor or Ph.D.) in law, and must be licensed to practice law in at least one state. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience in business law, estate planning, wealth management, or related fields. Prior teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, particularly in a college of business. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and the ability to effectively communicate complex legal and business concepts to students. Relevant professional credentials, licenses, or certifications, including admission to a state bar, Certified Financial Planner (CFP), or other credentials related to the position. Experience in curriculum development, student engagement, or professional service. Contact Info David Orozco , J.D. Bank of America Professor of Business Administration Herbert Wertheim College of Business Florida State University University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63794&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist – Employee Services (NHMFL)",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist – Employee Services (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63794 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace environment and employee-centered values. Responsibilities This position coordinates international hiring, onboarding, and compliance activities for NHMFL Employee Services. Manages visa processes, export control reviews, employment eligibility, and related documentation while supporting international employees and university partners. Key Responsibilities: Coordinates international hiring for A&P, USPS, Faculty, OPS, and courtesy appointments. Reviews hiring actions for compliance, processes offers in OMNI, prepares offer letters and salary documentation, and ensures required approvals are obtained. Manages Smart Onboarding requirements through completion and serves as a resource to hiring managers, coordinators, and candidates regarding international employment processes. Serves as the primary contact for immigration-related employment matters at the MagLab. Coordinates J-1, H-1B, & Green Card visa applications, extensions, renewals, and amendments in collaboration with university immigration offices. Reviews eligibility and documentation, tracks visa and employment authorization deadlines, maintains immigration records, and provides guidance to employees and departments to ensure continued compliance with federal requirements. Administers export control reviews for international hires and visitors through RAMP. Initiates and monitors submissions, collects required documentation, coordinates with departments, candidates, and compliance offices, and processes amendments as needed. Coordinates I-9 and employment eligibility verification for international employees, including required reverifications. Tracks authorization expiration dates, maintains accurate immigration, hiring, onboarding, and compliance records, and assists with audits, reporting, and compliance reviews. Provides operational support to the employee services team and backup assistance for domestic recruitment and hiring. Assists with special projects, process improvements, and administrative initiatives. Collaborates with employee services staff, departments, and university partners to improve services and efficiency while providing responsive support for HR-related inquiries. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Minimum salary of $43,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63525&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Community Health Worker (OPS) Walton County, Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine",
      "description": "Community Health Worker (OPS) Walton County, Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63525 Location Walton County, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Rural Health Transformation Program - College of Medicine Florida State University’s College of Medicine has been awarded more than $19 million through the Rural Health Transformation Program to strengthen healthcare access and outcomes in rural Florida. The funding will support six new projects focused on critical needs including behavioral health, preventive care, food insecurity, telehealth, at-home care and healthcare workforce development. Through partnerships with communities and healthcare organizations across Northwest and Southwest Florida, FSU is working to bring innovative, practical solutions directly to rural communities and help close longstanding gaps in care. Responsibilities Conduct health needs screenings and care navigation at every mobile unit stop. Will travel throughout Walton County attending mobile clinic events, visiting local clinics, interacting with community paramedicine providers, and ensuring patients are connected to the resources they require. Initiate and track referrals to Community Paramedicine, Remote Patient Telemonitoring, Retail Clinic Services and fixed-site primary care providers. Confirm appointment completion and document barriers to follow-through. Connect patients to local health and human services resources including WIC, transportation assistance, and social support programs. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalency and two years of experience. Valid FL or GA driver's license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Community Health Worker Certification (CHWC) must be achieved within the first year of employment. Preferred Qualifications Ability to adhere to ethical business practices, promote ethical behavior, and represent the University in appointed area as required. Ability to demonstrate effective customer service skills and establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing and gather, interpret, report, and/or edit information. Ability to perform accurately in a detail-oriented environment and prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously. Ability to maintain accurate records and retrieve files from active or archive sources. Basic filing practices to include numeric and alphabetic systems. Helpful This role will be the primary accountability bridge across five Rural Health Transformation Program initiatives (in Walton County, FL) that form a network to expand access to preventive and primary care services for rural populations. The initiatives are (1) mobile health, (2) on-site pharmacy/retail clinic services, (3) community paramedicine, (4) remote patient telemonitoring and (5) health information exchange. Contact Info Georgia Arnold University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $19 – $24 per hour, commensurate with education/experience. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is a full time OPS/temporary job located in Walton County, Florida (2 hours west of Tallahassee). Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position will be responsible for traveling throughout Walton County several days per week and will support Bundle 1 - Preventative Care & Care At Home Northwest region, which is defined as Bay, Calhoun, Escambia, Franklin, Gadsden, Gulf, Holmes, Jackson, Jefferson, Leon, Liberty, Okaloosa, Santa Rosa, Wakulla, Walton, Washington on the Rural Health Transformation Program Map . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Schedule: Generally the hours are 8:00 am - 5:00 pm, but will very depending on community activities. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63797&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Custodial Worker (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63797 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance and Administration About Us | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise or information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/. Responsibilities Perform general duties including sweep, mop, vacuum, wax, and polish VCT floors with floor machines; dust and clean furniture, walls, rails, windows, sills, and blinds; empty waste baskets, remove refuse and trash up to 25 pounds from building; clean, sanitize, and restock restrooms; move furniture as needed to accomplish assigned duties. Assist with indoor and outdoor special set-ups and break-downs for classes or functions on campus. Respond to emergency clean-ups as needed; assist with Facilities, Operations, and Maintenance Department functions and activities as needed; other duties as required by supervisor. Qualifications Completion of ninth grade. Ability to meet the physical requirements of the position, such as reaching, bending, lifting, pushing, and pulling while performing cleaning duties. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of the practices and procedures of custodial work. Good communication and customer service skills. Work well independently or in a team environment. Helpful During the first three months, the custodian will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with the campus, tools, and safety procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor. By the end of the first 90 days, the custodian is expected to be confident in navigating campus facilities, performing routine cleaning procedures, and contributing independently to the department's work while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to David Gary for more information regarding this position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting in the lower $30,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The schedule for this position is Monday through Friday, 2pm to 10pm. This position is located in Panama City, Florida. This position will begin in Winter 2026 or earlier. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63804&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Deputy Athletic Director & Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "Deputy Athletic Director & Chief Financial Officer Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63804 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Athletics Responsibilities Serves as the chief financial strategist and executive operational leader for Intercollegiate Athletics. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Athletics, this role provides executive-level oversight for all financial planning, resource allocation, and business operations for the Athletics Department, Seminole Boosters and FSU Athletics Association. The Deputy AD/CFO acts as a fiduciary steward and strategic advisor, ensuring long-term financial sustainability while managing complex public university fund structures, central campus integrations, and a shifting NCAA revenue framework. Executive Leadership & Strategy: Serve as a core member of the Vice President for Athletics’ and the Seminole Boosters Executive Teams. Formulate and execute a multi-year financial sustainability plan aligned with Power-4 competitive realities. Act as the primary C-suite liaison to central university partners, including the University’s central Budget, Procurement, and Controller’s offices. Serve as the Treasurer for the FSU Athletics Association, Inc. Engage with audit and finance committees for various Boards of Directors. Financial Management & Budgeting: Direct the formulation, management, and monthly tracking of a $200M+ multi-disciplinary annual consolidated operating budget across core revenues. Design advanced financial models to evaluate department-wide ROIs, team-specific operations, and potential cost-containment measures. Approve and oversee financial proposals for new FTEs, coaching contracts, and multi-year employment agreements. Revenue Sharing & NIL: Manage the deployment of the department's direct-to-athlete revenue-sharing framework under current NCAA regulations and legal settlements. Collaborate with external partners and associated collectives to optimize Name, Image, and Likeness (NIL) strategy, corporate sponsorships, and multimedia rights revenues. Compliance, Auditing & Public Reporting: Ensure strict compliance with public institution accounting standards (GASB), state procurement regulations, and central university policies. Direct the preparation and filing of mandatory external reports, including annual NCAA Financial Reports, the Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act (EADA) report, and annual audited financial statements. Capital Infrastructure & Debt Management: Oversee financial strategy and funding mechanisms for major facility projects, coordinating debt issuance, bond covenants, and donor-gift tracking. Monitor capital project cash flows. Administrative & Business Operations: Directly supervise the Athletics Department and Seminole Boosters Business Offices. Establish clear internal controls and financial training programs for coaches, sport administrators, and support staff. Qualifications Master's degree and five years’ of related experience, or a bachelor’s degree and seven years of the same experience. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Financial Disclosure: This position requires annual Financial Disclosure based on Florida Statutes 112.3144 and 112.3145. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
